['shared responsibility','A team hosts a VM in IaaS and discovers its guest OS missed critical patches. Which party should normally remediate it?','The customer patches the guest OS; the provider patches the underlying cloud infrastructure.','Wait for the provider to patch every customer VM.','Switch regions without patching the guest.','IaaS leaves guest operating system administration with the customer; check the contract and service details for the exact boundary.'],
['service model','A small team wants to deploy code without managing operating-system patching. Which model most directly reduces that burden?','A managed PaaS runtime, after reviewing its supported controls and limitations.','Bare-metal colocation with customer-managed OSs.','IaaS VMs with all maintenance left to the team.','PaaS delegates more of the platform stack to the provider, while the customer remains responsible for code, identity, data and configuration.'],
['deployment model','A company needs some systems on premises and some in public cloud, with controlled connectivity between them. Which architecture is this?','A hybrid cloud architecture.','A single-tenant SaaS deployment.','A community cloud with no interconnection.','Hybrid cloud combines distinct environments; connectivity, identity, data flows and operational boundaries must be governed.'],
['multi-cloud','A company uses two cloud providers to reduce dependency on one vendor. What new security need becomes especially important?','Consistent identity, policy and monitoring across providers.','Assuming controls are identical by default.','Creating separate unmanaged administrator accounts.','Multi-cloud can reduce concentration risk but increases configuration and governance complexity.'],
['essential characteristics','An application can automatically add resources during demand spikes. Which cloud characteristic is being used?','Rapid elasticity.','Measured service.','Broad network access.','Rapid elasticity allows resources to scale out or in as workload demand changes.'],
['virtualization boundary','A cloud customer configures a virtual network and a provider operates the physical fabric. Where should the customer focus its own network controls?','Virtual routing, security groups, segmentation and exposed service paths.','Physical switch firmware in the provider data center.','Only the application’s color scheme.','The customer normally controls virtual networking settings while the provider manages physical infrastructure.'],
['architecture tradeoff','A workload must keep operating during one availability-zone failure. Which design decision best supports that objective?','Distribute redundant components across independent zones and test failover.','Place every component in one zone to simplify operations.','Rely only on a larger instance size.','Zone redundancy addresses a zone-level failure; verify dependencies and test recovery rather than assuming it works.'],
['shared tenancy','A risk review asks how unrelated customers are separated on shared infrastructure. What should be assessed?','Provider isolation mechanisms, customer configuration and the relevant service boundary.','Whether the provider advertises a large number of regions.','Whether the customers have the same billing cycle.','Multi-tenancy requires evaluating isolation at the layers relevant to the service and its configuration.'],
['service selection','A workload contains sensitive data and the team has limited operating capacity. What is the sound way to choose between IaaS and SaaS?','Compare business requirements, security obligations, provider controls and the team’s ability to operate each model.','Always choose IaaS because it provides the most customer control.','Always choose SaaS because it removes every customer security duty.','Service-model decisions are risk and capability decisions; neither model automatically makes a workload secure.'],
['cloud migration','Before moving a legacy system to cloud, what should the architect establish first?','Workload dependencies, data sensitivity, threat assumptions and target security requirements.','The final instance size only.','A public IP address for every component.','A migration plan should begin with business, data, dependency and security requirements.'],
['API control plane','An administrator can create public storage and change IAM policies from a cloud console. What is this console part of?','The cloud management plane, which needs strong access control and audit.','The data plane only.','The provider’s physical cooling plane.','The control or management plane governs configuration and can have broad impact, so secure it as a high-value attack surface.'],
['container distinction','A team claims containers eliminate the need to harden hosts because each container is isolated. What is the best response?','Containers share underlying components and still require host, image, runtime and privilege controls.','The claim is correct for every container platform.','Only application passwords matter in a container.','Containers provide useful isolation but are not automatically equivalent to separate physical systems.'],
['cloud economics','A proposed architecture duplicates all data across regions without a recovery requirement. What should happen before implementation?','Confirm availability and recovery objectives, data rules, cost and failure assumptions.','Duplicate first and document later.','Disable encryption to offset the storage cost.','Resilience choices should follow agreed RTO/RPO, residency and business requirements.'],
['portability','A company wants the option to move an application between providers. Which step helps most?','Document dependencies and use portable interfaces where practical, with tested export and migration plans.','Assume provider-specific services are interchangeable.','Avoid maintaining deployment documentation.','Portability depends on real dependencies, data formats, contracts and tested exit procedures.'],
['cloud terminology','A customer provisions resources through an API and receives a usage bill. Which characteristic combines these behaviors?','On-demand self-service and measured service.','Resource pooling and fixed capacity only.','Private connectivity and dedicated staff.','Self-service provisioning and metered usage are core cloud characteristics.']
