['vendor due diligence','A cloud vendor provides a current certification but no answers about the customer’s specific data path. What is the best next step?','Request scoped evidence and assess the service, data flow and shared responsibilities.','Approve the service based on the logo alone.','Assume the certification covers every configuration.','A certification is one evidence source; due diligence must address the actual service and use.'],
['control testing','A control is documented but no one has tested whether it works. What is the gap?','Operating effectiveness has not been demonstrated.','The control is automatically effective because it is written down.','The control needs a new name.','Design documentation alone does not prove that a control operates as intended.'],
['risk register','A team discovers a new cloud concentration risk but has not assigned an owner. What should happen?','Record it with context, accountable owner, treatment and review date.','Wait until a provider outage occurs.','Remove the service from inventory.','A risk register supports accountability and follow-through.'],
['continuous compliance','A cloud configuration can change daily. What assessment method best fits?','Continuous or frequent automated checks supplemented by periodic independent review.','One audit at initial deployment only.','No checks after the first certification.','Dynamic environments need ongoing monitoring as well as formal assurance activities.'],
['contract assurance','A contract lacks breach-notification timing. What is the best action before onboarding sensitive data?','Resolve the notification obligation and escalation process in contract or approved terms.','Assume notification will happen immediately.','Rely on a general marketing statement.','Incident notification must be contractually clear enough to support legal and response timelines.'],
['risk acceptance','A business executive wants to accept a high risk but lacks delegated authority. What should the security lead do?','Escalate through the approved risk-acceptance process to an authorized decision-maker.','Record the risk as accepted anyway.','Let the provider accept it for the customer.','Risk acceptance must be made by the correct authority and documented.'],
['assessment independence','A control owner self-certifies a high-impact control with no evidence. What would improve confidence?','Independent testing using defined criteria and verifiable evidence.','A more confident email from the same owner.','Removing the control from audit scope.','Independent, evidence-based testing reduces bias and supports reliable conclusions.']
